<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply up $3.0 mln in March 24 wk.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply up $3.0 mln in March 24 wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply rose $3.0 billion in the March 24 week to $3,880.2 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure rose $6.6 billion to $5,015.7 billion. M-1 fell $4.4 billion to $1,068.0 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,875.7 billion versus $3,873.0 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
